```apex
public with sharing class AccountCountrySync {

    /**
     * When an Account's BillingCountry changes, propagate the new value to the
     * MailingCountry of its Contacts whose MailingCountry is blank or still
     * equal to the Account's previous BillingCountry. Contacts who work abroad
     * (any other MailingCountry) and Contacts of unchanged Accounts are left
     * untouched.
     *
     * Bulk-safe: exactly one SOQL query and one DML statement per invocation,
     * and that query is filtered to the affected Accounts so it never tries to
     * read the entire Contact table.
     */
    public static void syncContactCountries(
        Map<Id, Account> oldMap,
        Map<Id, Account> newMap
    ) {
        // accountId -> new BillingCountry (only for accounts whose country changed)
        Map<Id, String> newCountryByAccount = new Map<Id, String>();
        // accountId -> old BillingCountry
        Map<Id, String> oldCountryByAccount = new Map<Id, String>();

        for (Account acc : newMap.values()) {
            String oldCountry = oldMap.get(acc.Id).BillingCountry;
            String newCountry = acc.BillingCountry;

            // Detect a genuine change (null-safe).
            if (oldCountry != newCountry) {
                newCountryByAccount.put(acc.Id, newCountry);
                oldCountryByAccount.put(acc.Id, oldCountry);
            }
        }

        if (newCountryByAccount.isEmpty()) {
            return; // No relevant change in this batch.
        }

        // One query, filtered to the changed accounts and the eligible contacts.
        // This replaces the unfiltered "SELECT ... FROM Contact" (see class/PR
        // notes): an unfiltered query would exceed the 50k row / heap limits on
        // an org with millions of contacts.
        List<Contact> contactsToUpdate = new List<Contact>();

        for (Contact con : [
            SELECT Id, AccountId, MailingCountry
            FROM Contact
            WHERE AccountId IN :newCountryByAccount.keySet()
        ]) {
            String oldCountry = oldCountryByAccount.get(con.AccountId);
            String newCountry = newCountryByAccount.get(con.AccountId);

            Boolean mailingBlank = String.isBlank(con.MailingCountry);
            Boolean matchesOld = con.MailingCountry == oldCountry;

            if (mailingBlank || matchesOld) {
                con.MailingCountry = newCountry;
                contactsToUpdate.add(con);
            }
        }

        if (!contactsToUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update contactsToUpdate;
        }
    }
}
```

A couple of notes on the logic:

- **"Blank or equal to the previous country"** is handled with `String.isBlank` (covers both `null` and empty string) OR an exact match on the old value. A contact with any other `MailingCountry` fails both tests and is skipped — exactly your "they work abroad" case.
- **Only changed accounts** are considered, because `newCountryByAccount` is only populated when `oldCountry != newCountry`, so contacts of unchanged accounts are never even queried.
- One `SELECT` and one `update` for the entire 200‑record batch keeps it within governor limits and free of queries/DML in loops.

